From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Exo data control, the clipboard for Linux apps without the focus

Linux apps get data control: ext_data_control_manager_v1 (wayland-
protocols, staging) and zwlr_data_control_manager_v1 (wlroots' protocol,
the same requests and events, for apps that know only that one), as on KDE
and wlroots desktops. A client sets ChromeOS's clipboard without the
keyboard focus, and is offered the clipboard each time it changes.

Dresden, 2026-11-09: copying in 1Password (Flatpak) did nothing. On
NickelOS 1Password's window is Electron on Wayland, whose own clipboard
works (GTK's does too), but 1Password copies through its Rust core: at
Ctrl+C that opens a Wayland connection of its own, binds wl_seat, looks for
a data-control manager, finds none, and gives up (WAYLAND_DEBUG on a test
PC). Password managers copy this way, and so do wl-copy and wl-paste in a
terminal.

- components/exo/wayland/nickel_data_control.cc: sources are Exo
  DataSources whose delegate accepts any surface, or none, as the focused
  one; Seat::SetSelection reads them into ChromeOS's clipboard as it reads
  a wl_data_source. Devices watch ChromeOS's clipboard
  (ui::ClipboardMonitor) and send each new content as an offer (Exo's
  DataOffer over the clipboard). set_selection with no source clears the
  clipboard (a password manager clearing what it copied). The primary
  selection stays with zwp_primary_selection (set_primary_selection is
  ignored).
- Seat::SetSelection: whether a source may set the selection is its
  delegate's call (a wl_data_source still needs its client focused); with
  no focused surface, the clipboard's source endpoint is the default one.
- The protocols: GN targets for ext-data-control-v1.xml (in the tree) and
  wlr-data-control-unstable-v1.xml (wlr-protocols, MIT, added under
  third_party/wayland-protocols/wlr/); both on the standard list Linux
  apps see (Chrome 0029).

What any Linux app can now do, as on KDE: read the clipboard while it
changes, without being in front.

